#rebase: git rebase -i (interactive rebase) lets you edit, reorder, combine, split, drop, or reword commits. It's one of the most powerful Git commands for cleaning up commit history before sharing it.

1. git rebase -i <hash/head~n>
2. vim is opened, press i to enter interactive mode
3. use commands to do what u want to do with commits
4. esc, shift wq
5. git rebase --continue
